+1.1 Write $p=\Pr(\text{score}<v)$ for an incumbent. The good/bad decomposition of $V|0\rangle$ has amplitudes $\sin\theta=\sqrt p$ and $\cos\theta=\sqrt{1-p}$. Multiplication of the two reflection matrices gives the usual rotation by $2\theta$, so after $q$ iterates the success probability is $\sin^2((2q+1)\theta)$. The normalized good projection has the same pure-state ray for every positive-probability good branch by [F2]; a possible scalar phase does not change its measurement distribution. Hence every verified improvement, whether direct or amplified, has the original distribution conditioned on score < incumbent. For $0<p<1$, summing the geometric progression of $e^{4iq\theta}$ gives the random-iteration average $1/2-\sin(4K\theta)/(4K\sin(2\theta))$. [F1, F2, given, algebra]
 
